# BeforeCode

This repository plans its work with BeforeCode (`bfc`). Every change is made against a Plan: a short `intent.md` written by a person and a `plan.md` written for agents, with acceptance criteria `AC-1`, `AC-2`, …

## How to work with bfc

- The user works in the TUI (`bfc` without arguments) and does not run the CLI. You run it, with `--json` where you read.
- Commands you may use:
  - `bfc prime [id]`: these instructions and the Current plan.
  - `bfc show [id] --json`: one plan with `intent.md`, `plan.md`, its acceptance criteria, open Questions and every Message (`messages`).
  - `bfc list --json` and `bfc search <text>`: find plans.
  - `bfc ask <id> --to <email|ai> [--ref plan.md#AC-n] -m <text>`: ask a Question.
  - `bfc reply <message-ULID> -m <text>`: answer a Question; add `--verbatim` when you record the user's own words.
  - `bfc start <id>`: only when the user asks to work on a plan; it switches the branch, which makes the plan the Current plan.
  - `bfc ready [id] --json` and `bfc claim [id] [T-n] --json`: list the open Tasks of approved plans, and take one before you work on it; the first Claim wins, so when it fails, take another.
  - `bfc handoff [id] T-n -m <what is done, what comes next> [--done]`: before you stop working on a Task you hold, hand it off: `--done` when it is finished, else it is Paused for the next one. Then run `bfc push`.
- Gates are for people: `submit`, `approve`, `request-changes`, `withdraw` and `close` refuse to run inside an agent, and so does `acknowledge`. When a plan needs one, tell the user to open `bfc` and take it there.
- Edits need an approved plan: a hook blocks file edits unless the Current plan is `approved`. Do not change code before that.
- Implement `plan.md` as approved. When the work must depart from it, record the deviation with `bfc ask <id> --to <plan author email> --ref plan.md#AC-n -m <what and why>` and tell the user.

